{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PhiQTowerJsjBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PhiQTowerJsjBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.PhiQJSJ","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.skeletonBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.skeletonBridge","kind":"instance","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge.lean#L90-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridgeAxiom.bridge_per_piece","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridgeAxiom.bridge_per_piece","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The missing input for the bridge per piece. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridgeAxiom.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridgeAxiom.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridgeAxiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridgeAxiom","kind":"class","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge.lean#L76-L86","doc":"**Skeleton `PerPieceBridge` instance.**  The `bridge_per_piece`\nfield equates `0 = rho q * pieceVolume q β S`.  Since\n`pieceVolume` is itself `sorry` (the upstream Kashaev conjecture's\ndeferred per-piece value), this equation is also a deferred\n`sorry` — the conjectural input proper.  Per AGENTS.md §3b, a\n`sorry` inside an instance field is understood as the conjecture,\nnot missing proof.  Discharges §3b-cond for downstream consumers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.skeletonRealisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.skeletonRealisation","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge.lean#L51-L74","doc":"**Skeleton `TowerSummandRealization` witness.**  Defines the\narchimedean realisation as constant zero.  Trivially non-negative;\nencodes none of the actual realisation infrastructure.\n\n**Demoted from `instance` to `def`, 2026-08-24.**  The class docstring\nabove says it is \"populated by any concrete instance of the realisation\nfunctor\" — but as a global `instance` this zero skeleton *preempted* that:\ntypeclass resolution satisfied every `[TowerSummandRealization q]` binder\nin this file from it, so `bridge` and `bridge_nonneg` read as claims about\nan arbitrary realisation while the only realisation in scope was `0`.\nUnder that resolution `PerPieceBridgeAxiom.bridge_per_piece` reads\n`0 = rho q * pieceVolume q β S`, i.e. it asserts `pieceVolume ≡ 0` for\n`q > 1` — the block comment below already noticed this and recorded it as\nexpected.\n\nThis is the `triv_hecke` / `triv_wedderburn` shape demoted in PR #5581 for\nthe same reason. As a `def` the degenerate model stays available to anyone\nwho wants to name it (`letI := skeletonRealisation q`), which is the honest\nuse — witnessing that the class is inhabited, so the conditional theorems\nare not vacuously true — without standing in for the real realisation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}